<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tributum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tributum was a direct tax in ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Originally a levy on Roman citizens to fund war, it was suspended for citizens in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> after 167 BCE, and under the empire the term came to denote taxes on provincial land and persons. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> discuss it as part of the fiscal system that financed the army and imperial administration.</p></div>
